# hatch_and_diagonal_blanks.xlsx -- FROZEN EXPECTATION.
# A reading of the openpyxl-authored fixture against plan 01 D2/D3/D4.
# Corrected ONLY when that reading was wrong -- never edited to chase an FSA1 regression.
#
# The reading, in three steps:
#
# 1. `cellXfs` states four entries. `A1` carries no `s=` at all; `B1` is `s="1"` -> fillId 2 ->
#    `<patternFill patternType="solid"><fgColor rgb="FF00B0F0"/>`; `D4` is `s="2"` -> fillId 1 ->
#    `<patternFill patternType="gray125"/>`; `E5` is `s="3"` -> borderId 1 -> `<diagonal style="thin">`
#    and no left/right/top/bottom edge. The one `<font>` is Calibri 11 under `<color theme="1"/>`, so
#    the Normal font and the text colour are both the format's own default and neither is declared.
#
# 2. OCCUPANCY is `A1`, which holds a value, plus every blank whose look a RULE CAN CARRY. `B1`'s
#    solid fill spells `background-color`, so `B1` is content. `D4`'s hatch and `E5`'s diagonal are
#    dropped and named below -- an appearance no declaration carries is by definition not carried, so
#    it cannot occupy a coordinate the export would then come back without. Occupancy is therefore the
#    two coordinates A1 and B1: a bounding box of 2 cells with nothing wasted, so ONE block A1:B1.
#
# 3. One row is the whole block, so the fill is a COLUMN rule; column 2 of 2 is `td:last-child`.
#    `A1` states no fill, so no bare `td` may claim one.
#
# The two losses are named in the sheet's own reading order, D4 before E5. They are named at all
# because the sheet still HOLDS those coordinates: a look the source draws over an empty cell keeps
# its cell inside the sheet's extent even where no rule can carry it, which is what separates "not
# occupancy" from "dropped in silence".
warning: gray125 pattern fill at Blanks!D4 dropped
warning: diagonal border at Blanks!E5 dropped
file: Blanks/@presentation.css
|@scope (A1:B1) {
|  td:last-child { background-color: #00b0f0 }
|}
|
file: Blanks/A1:B1
|kept	
